  "notes": "The noun form of {企|たくら}む (to plot/scheme). Almost always carries a negative connotation of deception or malicious intent.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {企|たくら}みを{見抜|みぬ}く: to see through a scheme\n- {企|たくら}みが{露見|ろけん}する: a plot is exposed\n- {恐|おそ}ろしい{企|たくら}み: a terrible plot\n- {企|たくら}みに{加|くわ}わる: to join in a conspiracy\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {陰謀|いんぼう}: conspiracy — larger scale, often political\n- {策略|さくりゃく}: stratagem — can be neutral, more calculated\n- {計画|けいかく}: plan — neutral, no negative connotation",
